                <pb facs="0753" n="637" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg637"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.51/676.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Buckner</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 26, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. Clark’s January 25. Yes, bankers consider that maintenance police force
                    essential to proper collection customs, and that article 4, agreement, gives
                    authority to pay force as one of first liens against assigned revenues.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
